    "title": "Spend the 2.5x throughput on deeper exploration instead of more shallow runs",
    "description": "Merged HEAD now completes ~1360 runs/s where baseline did ~615, but meanPrefixDepth (3.30) and maxPrefixDepth (8) are unchanged and 72% of runs end in iterationsExhausted rather than planComplete, meaning the extra speed is being spent on more copies of the same shallow prefixes. Add an arm that reinvests the surplus: raise the per-run step budget (stepBudgetSum currently 6000/run, stepsUsedSum ~76% of it) and/or the prefix-depth cap in scheduler_configs/loop/general_vr.json, holding wall-clock exposure fixed, and compare h1-h4 rates and depthAtLeast tails against the current config at equal exposure. Gated by the existing per-run step-budget and depth-cap config fields; no new mechanism.",
